{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515051-fake-bodies","id":1515051,"title":"Fake bodies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-14T19:32:16-07:00","id":1515051,"title":"Fake bodies","content":"This is about a hypothetical cross-over scenario between MtA and DtF, and if a mage created a body for a fallen one, let's not think about the reasons for now, as it would be, at first glance I would think he should use Matter 4 or 5 to create a human body for him, but since the body must be alive for him to use it then use Life 5 instead? Another option I think would be to use Matter 4 to make a lifeless body and then create life in it using Prime 5, then it still lacks the mind, so do we use Mind 4 to form a consciousness or do we also need Prime for that? Another option would be to transfer a person's memories into this new body so Correspondence + Mind I guess. What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T02:32:57-07:00","id":1515076,"title":"","content":"HDYDT addresses this on pp 24\u201325: for an artificially created human, you need Life 5 (for the body), Mind 5 (for the mind), Spirit 5 (for the soul), and Prime 2 (for the \u201cspark of life\u201d). There's a simpler Life 5/Spirit 4/Prime 2 option that would let you create a \u201cflesh bag\u201d for the demon to Possess (and even the need for Spirit 4 is questionable if the demon does the work of Possessing its new body); but I'd say that the result of anything short of Life 5/Mind 5/Spirit 5/Prime 2 would be more akin to an Earthbound than to a Fallen. <br /> <br /> On top of that, creating complex life forms is considered to be an Outlandish Feat: ten to twenty successes to pull off (M20 p.502). Throwing in an artificial mind and soul is likely to bump that up into the realm of Godlike Feats. Even as an Outlandish Feat, that puts it firmly in Great Work territory (M20 p.542). As well, Outlandish and God-Like Feats have their Difficulty increased (M20 p.503). Since the base Difficulty of a Sphere 5 Effect is between 8 and 10, you're definitely going to need to work the Magical Modifiers if you want to stand a chance of success.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T07:15:47-07:00","id":1515115,"title":"","content":"On another thread I've been commenting on how on how Prime is arbitrarily added for things like &quot;spark of life&quot; that are never mentioned or even hinted at in the Prime writeup. Fortunately in this case mage's also need Prime 2 for creation of the body so it is a moot point.<br /> <br /> It's been a while since I read Demon, what are the mind and soul doing in this context? Providing consent? Morality/Humanity?\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T08:23:17-07:00","id":1515131,"title":"","content":"Soul would not be necessary since the fallen one can do all the functions of it, however the body he occupies is normal and therefore needs a mind to function, another problem is the memories, the fallen ones have access to all knowledge and abilities of the body they occupy and that's even how they know how to speak and understand the human language, so in addition to needing a mind to function, they also need it to have enough information to mix and interact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T08:46:13-07:00","id":1515134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515051-fake-bodies?p=1515131#post1515131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soul would not be necessary since the fallen one can do all the functions of it, however the body he occupies is normal and therefore needs a mind to function, another problem is the memories, the fallen ones have access to all knowledge and abilities of the body they occupy and that's even how they know how to speak and understand the human language, so in addition to needing a mind to function, they also need it to have enough information to mix and interact.</div> </div> </div> </div>In that case, I\u2019d go with Life 5/Mind 5/Prime 2. Mind 4 lets you create memories, but you still need the full 5 ranks to create a mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515051-fake-bodies?p=1515076#post1515076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> On top of that, creating complex life forms is considered to be an Outlandish Feat: ten to twenty successes to pull off (M20 p.502). Throwing in an artificial mind and soul is likely to bump that up into the realm of Godlike Feats. Even as an Outlandish Feat, that puts it firmly in Great Work territory (M20 p.542). As well, Outlandish and God-Like Feats have their Difficulty increased (M20 p.503). Since the base Difficulty of a Sphere 5 Effect is between 8 and 10, you're definitely going to need to work the Magical Modifiers if you want to stand a chance of success.</div> </div> </div> </div>That one seemed off to me, so I tried to dig into the reasons. It seems arbitrary that it should take 10+ successes to make a human body when it only takes 4 to turn a grasshopper into a human body. It shouldn't be fundamentally more complicated to create a body from quintessence than to create one from another body.<br /> <br /> And indeed, on closer look it isn't. While it would only be four successes to create that human body from a grasshopper, if we want it to have a more or less indefinite duration, we have to add 6+ more successes, which brings the spell up to 10+. The two are almost the same spell. They only differ in what the body is created from.<br /> <br /> Considered this way, it is only an Impressive feat with an extended duration. It\u2019s not clear if the Outlandish/Godlike penalty comes from the difficulty of the base effect or from the total number of successes required, but I lean towards the former. I would not add the increased difficulty for Outlandish for creating a body.<br /> <br /> This also gives insight into the number of successes for the Life/Spirit/Mind/Prime spell. I would certainly put creating a mind, creating a soul, and creating a body in roughly the same range, success-wise: 4 successes. However, I would not triple the duration cost. So the overall effect would take:<br /> <br /> For body, mind, soul, and duration that\u2019s: 4 + 4 + 4 + 6+, so 18+ successes.<br /> For body, mind, and duration just 4 + 4 + 6+, so 14+ successes.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s still a lot of successes, but not into Godlike. Indeed, taking out the duration cost the full body, mind, soul package is an Outlandish 12 successes, and the lower body and mind package is only a Mighty 8.<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 06-15-2023, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T08:59:26-07:00","id":1515135,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, the \u201cspark of life\u201d thing isn't mentioned or hinted at under Prime; but it <i>is</i> mentioned under Life \u2014 or rather, under the description of Life Patterns, which talks about how Life Patterns have a trickle of Quintessence flowing through them. It's not the way I'd do it (if I had my way, the Spheres in 5e would get a rewrite similar to Awakened's Arcana); but there it is. <br /> <br /> DtF talks about how when a demon from the Abyss possesses a human host, its contact with the human soul causes the change in the demon that sets it apart from the evil demons that lack a conscience (called \u201cEarthbound demons\u201d in DtF). So at the very least, if you want a Fallen demon instead of an Earthbound demon, you'll need both a body and a soul. I'd have to double-check about the mind; though if I recall correctly, that provides the demon with basic familiarity with the modern world, as well as things like knowing how to walk and talk, and other information needed to slip into the person's social situation (e.g., recognizing acquaintances, etc.). <br /> <br /> DtF gets around the moral conundrum of stealing someone's life by having the demon possess someone whose life is basically over: either the person has actually just died, and the demon possesses the person just before the soul disappears from the body; or the person has essentially become suicidal or non-functional. In short: without the demon's intervention, the host would either be dead already or would soon be dead. So instead of stealing a life, the demon is now providing a new lease on life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T07:17:04-07:00","id":1515366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515051-fake-bodies?p=1515135#post1515135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For what it's worth, the \u201cspark of life\u201d thing isn't mentioned or hinted at under Prime; but it <i>is</i> mentioned under Life \u2014 or rather, under the description of Life Patterns, which talks about how Life Patterns have a trickle of Quintessence flowing through them. It's not the way I'd do it (if I had my way, the Spheres in 5e would get a rewrite similar to Awakened's Arcana); but there it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I\u2019ve seen the \u201cflow of quintessence\u201d used to describe other patterns too, though I\u2019d have to look. By default, transmutations from one pattern to another do not need Prime and that includes changing a stone to a human. The only example I can think of that indicates a \u201cspark of life\u201d ability is animating corpses and skeletons, and there\u2019s not an explanation of the thinking there. So whether they were intentional, misguided, or remnants of a former ruleset is hard to say.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}